  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Marketplace-wide seller observability",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 3,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## Petabyte — Marketplace Sellers\nMarketplace-wide view of an **ephemeral** seller GPU fleet. Sellers connect / disconnect / reboot / vanish freely; the platform observes them **only from the agent's authenticated outbound calls** (`/heartbeat`, `/jobs/next`, result upload). **Prometheus never scrapes seller machines** and sellers open **no inbound ports**. Offline is detected from **heartbeat expiry** — a stale spec drops out of supply automatically. History survives a GPU going offline: logs/metrics/traces live on the observability server and job/ledger rows stay in Postgres.\n\nAll gauges/counters here use **bounded labels only — no seller id is ever a Prometheus label**. Per-seller detail (uptime, completion / rejection / reconnect rates, validation failures, trust score, earnings, payout state) is **high-cardinality** and is queried by `seller_id` in **Loki logs / the DB**, not from Prometheus."
      },
      "datasource": null
    },
